    "title": "Holyoke police seize loaded stolen firearm, drugs from vehicle - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By John Budenas ,\n7 hours ago\nHOLYOKE, Mass. (WWLP) - Holyoke police arrested two men Tuesday after officers say they found a loaded, stolen firearm and multiple drugs inside a vehicle in a Maple Street parking lot.\nTwo arrested after police find firearm, heroin in Springfield traffic stop Holyoke Police Chief Brian Keenan said officers responded at about 11 a.m. Tuesday to 378 Maple St., where Officer Andrew Gruska located a vehicle with two occupants that was allegedly trespassing in a parking lot.\nGruska was later assisted by Sgt. John Veit and Officer Thomas Spafford during the investigation.\nPolice said officers found a loaded firearm, four bundles containing 40 bags of heroin, cocaine, eight Suboxone strips, two gabapentin pills and a loose round of ammunition inside the vehicle.\n(Courtesy of Holyoke Police Department) The firearm was reported stolen from Bristol, Connecticut, and was loaded with nine rounds of ammunition, according to police.\nThe driver, 42-year-old Benjamin Santos of Holyoke, and passenger, 36-year-old Alberto Munoz of Springfield, were both arrested.\n36-year-old Alberto Munoz of Springfield is charged with:\n• Carrying a Loaded Firearm without a License\n• Possession of a Firearm without an FID Card\n• Possession of a Firearm During the Commission of a Felony\n• Improper Storage of a Firearm\n• Possession of Ammunition without an FID Card\n• Receiving Stolen Property Less than $1200\n• Possession with the Intent to Distribute a Class A Drug\n• Possession of a Class A Drug\n• Possession of a Class B Drug (Two Counts)\n• Possession of a Class E Drug\n• Trespassing with a Motor Vehicle\nSantos faces the same charges, according to police.\nLocal News Headlines Vibra Hospital redevelopment sparks safety concerns Whalen supporters host debate watch party in downtown Springfield Springfield project among 5 awarded state tax credits to create 856 new homes MassDOT launches annual high school video contest focused on micromobility safety WWLP-22News, an NBC affiliate, began broadcasting in March 1953 to provide local news, network, syndicated, and local programming to western Massachusetts. Download the 22News Plus app on your TV to watch live-streaming newscasts and video on demand.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WWLP.",
    "summary": "(WWLP) - Holyoke police arrested two men Tuesday after officers say they found a loaded, stolen firearm and multiple drugs inside a vehicle in a Maple Street parking lot. Two arrested after police find firearm, heroin in Springfield traffic stop Holyoke Police Chief Brian Keenan said officers responded at about 11 a.m. Tuesday to 378 Maple St., where Officer Andrew Gruska located a vehicle with two occupants that was allegedly trespassing in a parking lot.",
